## Summary
A 26-year-old skier died in a tragic accident on the Ortles mountain in Alto Adige, Italy, at an altitude of approximately 3,700 meters along the steep Minnigerode canyon. The incident occurred near the 3,905-meter peak. The cause and circumstances of the accident are not specified in the provided article.

## Key Points
- Accident location: Ortles mountain, Alto Adige, Italy
- Altitude of incident: approximately 3,700 meters
- Location detail: Minnigerode canyon near the 3,905-meter peak
- Victim: 26-year-old skier (gender and name not specified)


